# Highlands Map (biome: highlands)
# Symbols (assets/tiles.yaml): . = grass  H = heather  S = stream
#   % = cliff  # = granite  B = ruined wall  = = slate wall
#   T = pine   A = rock outcrop  R = boulder  + = start
#   W = shallow water  Q = deep water (needs Walk on Water)
# Monster spawns: c=puma h=elf_archer j=elf_swordsman v=mountain_troll
#   z=archmage q=lich
#
# THE GREAT GLEN. One deep valley crosses the whole map west to east between
# two ragged cliff scarps (y17-18 and y32-33, each a staggered double band, so
# every step in them is a real notch, not a doorway). The glen is the LIVING
# part: the Kirn falls into it, the river runs down it past a standing-stone
# avenue into LOCH BRAE, and the loch drains out over the Linn to the south.
#
# FOUR NAMED CROSSINGS, nothing else gets through:
#   KIRN FALLS  (x12-13, y18) - the pinewood stream drops over the north scarp;
#     you climb beside the waterfall
#   THE OGRE STAIR (x28-29, y18) - the keep's road down its bluff into the glen
#   MOOR GATE   (x13-14, y33) - the shepherds' notch up to the stone circle
#   THE LINN    (x35-36, y32) - the loch's outflow falls south; a walkway
#     follows the water down to the meadow
#
# NORTH BAND (one connected upland, y1-16)
#   Pinewood (west): pine copses and lanes, elf archers; the CLOCK TOWER
#     facade is set in the crag along the top; the Kirn rises here (x12).
#   The WARDEN KEEP (centre, x19-29): granite outer court (gates north and
#     south), slate-and-ruin inner hall - mage tower, tavern, two archmages;
#     elf swordsmen hold the court corners. Its south gate leads to the Stair.
#   Grimscree (east): boulder-cluster fell, mountain trolls, and THE TOR
#     (x40-44) - the jump gate: stand at (42,4), vault the granite lip.
#
# THE GLEN (y19-31)
#   Kirn pool under the falls; the river east under a STANDING-STONE AVENUE
#   (x16-24, y20); TWIN SENTINELS at the west mouth; glen copses with archers;
#   LOCH BRAE (x35-44) filling the east end, with THE CRANNOG - an ancient
#   lake dwelling on deep water - holding a golden hoard.
#
# SOUTH BAND (y34-48)
#   The Heather Moor (west): the STONE CIRCLE (x3-7), the peat hag (x10-11,
#     y41-42), pumas; the MOUNTAIN PRISON block (x2-7, y40-42); the SHEEPFOLD
#     (x12-14, y45-47), a drystone pen with its gate north - a hiding pocket.
#   Brae Meadow (centre): the SAFE HUB - the river from the Linn runs past it
#     and out of the south wall at x24, where the forest passage arrives;
#     a WAYSTONE (stone-heather-stone) at (19-21,44).
#   The SLATE TOMB (east, x38-46): one north gate, a slate chamber, three
#     liches round the Lich Nexus and its tome; it stands over the strip where
#     the dragon-cliffs passage opens (x47-48, y42-44).
#
# CAPABILITY GATES - rewards only, never a route; Fly clears both.
# gate: jump (42,6) spell_lectern - the Tor shelf: stand (42,4), vault (42,5)
# gate: water (39,25) chest_golden - the crannog, wants Walk on Water
